_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**Rebuild discovery state after the follow set is actually mutated.**

`request_rebuild()` currently fires before `repos.follows.add()`, and only on the `newly_created` path. That means following an already-known user never refreshes discovery, and even a newly-created follow can be rebuilt against the pre-insert graph. `unfollow_user()` also skips the rebuild entirely, so stale follow edges can linger until some unrelated refresh happens.



<details>
<summary>♻️ Suggested fix</summary>

```diff
